@preamble let process = import("process")
start
@unchecked
Starts command with a list of string arguments. The child uses the Aiki runtime's current working directory and receives attached stdin, stdout, and stderr endpoints.

start(command, args)
===
stdin
@unchecked
Returns the process's writable stdin endpoint. Use io.write and io.close on it.

stdin(process)
===
stdout
@unchecked
Returns the process's readable stdout endpoint. Use io.read or io.read_line on it.

stdout(process)
===
stderr
@unchecked
Returns the process's readable stderr endpoint. Use io.read or io.read_line on it.

stderr(process)
===
wait
@unchecked
Waits for completion and returns the process exit code. Repeated waits return the same result.

wait(process)
===
terminate
@unchecked
Forcibly terminates a running child process. Portable graceful signaling is introduced separately by the signals phase.

terminate(process)
